<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Sheikhdom of Kalba</h1><p class="st-meta">1936 CE – 1951 CE · capital Kalba</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived Trucial sheikhdom on the Gulf of Oman coast, recognised by Britain in 1936 in exchange for an emergency airstrip.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kalba, a town on the east coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> peninsula, was ruled by a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qasimi">Al Qasimi</a> family as part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sheikhdom-of-sharjah">Sheikhdom of Sharjah</a>. In 1936 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> recognised its sheikh, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/said-bin-hamad-al-qasimi">Said bin Hamad Al Qasimi</a>, as an independent ruler among the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/trucial-states">Trucial States</a>, in return for permission to build an emergency landing ground for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperial-airways">Imperial Airways</a> flights to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The sheikhdom was tiny, living from fishing and date gardens. After Said's death in 1937 his young son succeeded under a regent, and the family's internal disputes, together with rival claims by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-fujairah">Fujairah</a>, left it unstable.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After a violent succession dispute in 1951, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> allowed Kalba to be reincorporated into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sheikhdom-of-sharjah">Sharjah</a>, and it remains part of that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sheikhdom-of-kalba.jpg" alt="Sheikhdom of Kalba" width="320" height="200"><figcaption>Image: Pointedstick · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kalbamangrove.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1936 CE – 1951 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kalba</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Said bin Hamad Al Qasimi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kalba, Emirate of Kalba</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1944&amp;focus=sheikhdom-of-kalba" aria-label="Sheikhdom of Kalba on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6175 1256 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sheikhdom of Kalba lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6495 1512L6439 1557M6495 1512L6468 1502"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6439 1557h0M6468 1502h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6495 1512h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6495 1512h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1944&amp;focus=sheikhdom-of-kalba">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
